Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) + 1 = RET);
</code>

This assert statement checks that the size of the ArrayList instance is increased by one after adding an object to it. This is the most relevant part of the provided code, as it's where an element is added to the list. The 'RET' represents the return value of the function, in this case, the index where the new item was inserted. The 'OLD(_size)' refers to the size of the list before the addition of the new item, ensuring that the list size has indeed increased by one. The assert statement checks that this equality holds, which would be true if the 'Add' method of the ArrayList class is implemented correctly.
